# The 584MB portable toolchain. Re-extract from the w64devkit release rather
# than committing it -- it is a third-party binary distribution, it dwarfs the
# project by four orders of magnitude, and build.ps1 only needs it on PATH.
#
# Excluded by PATH, not by `tools/`: the rest of that directory is source. The
# headless tests and the model/map editors under tools/*.c are as much a part
# of this project as src/ is, and a blanket `tools/` rule silently drops them.
tools/w64devkit/

# Build output. Everything here is regenerated by build.ps1.
build/
*.exe
*.o
*.map

# Baked assets: regenerated from assets/*.txt by bake.ps1 on every build, so
# committing it would mean a file that conflicts on every branch and that no
# human ever reads.
src/gen_assets.h

# Freedoom lumps downloaded by assets/sprites/import-freedoom.py. Upstream art
# in its original form: the PNGs the importer produces from it ARE committed,
# so nothing here is needed to build, and re-downloading is one command.
assets/sprites/.freedoom-cache/

# A contact sheet the importer writes with --preview, for looking at the
# conversion. Regenerated on demand and never read by the build.
assets/sprites/_preview.png

# Editor and OS noise.
.vs/
*.user
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
